@ Start

// Chapter 02 — second beat. Requires MelodiaQuillShorewake rev A, which sets the
// PERSISTENT session var melodia_shorewake_attuned (melodia_ prefix => survives
// save/reload via RestorePersistentQuillVariables). Non-persistent bridge flags
// (flag.* names) are deliberately NOT used as guards.

$ Background {&/Game/Melodia/UI/Textures/Figma/T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_CosmicOrrery.T_Melodia_Figma_Asset_Hero_CosmicOrrery} none 0

? if: {melodia_skiff_departed} == on

  - Sir Melodious
    The Starskiff has already kissed the far tide. The memory of its bells stays with us.

  $ End

? else:

  ? if: {melodia_shorewake_attuned} == on

    - Melusina
      The mooring bell is warm under my hand. The Shorewake hums against the current, ready.

    - Sir Melodious
      Two ways to say goodbye to a shore, little bard. One of them the sea remembers longer.

    * Play the departure phrase on the lyre first. | -> PlayPhrase
    * Push off quietly; the tide will not wait. | -> QuietPush

  ? else:

    - Sir Melodious
      The skiff is tethered, but the weave has not chosen you yet. Return when the shorewake sits easy on your shoulders.

    $ End

  ? endif

? endif

<@> PlayPhrase

- Melusina
  Then let the sea take a song with it. One phrase — no more. The wake should outlast the note.

- .
  (Lyre phrase sounds: three rising figures, the farewell motif.)

$ Notify melodia:stat:intent.skiffdeparture.farewell:melodia_resonance:3

-> Departure

<@> QuietPush

- Melusina
  Some goodbyes are just a hand on a rope and a held breath.

-> Departure

<@> Departure

- Sir Melodious
  Lines away. The terrace lamps are fireflies now. Steady — the high current runs cold on this side.

- Melusina
  Cold, and quiet, and mine. I think the sea was never calling my name. It was saving a seat.

$ melodia_skiff_departed = on

$ Notify melodia:questcomplete:quest.shorewake.passage:flag.shorewake.passage:reward.skiff_passage:intent.skiffdeparture.passage:checkpoint.skiff.underway

@ Finish

- .
  The Starskiff slides the last ribbon of shore and is sea, wholly. Chapter 02 onward.

$ End
